 "dispositions": [
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-DEFAULT-PUBLIC-CARRIER",
   "position": "agreed and corrected",
   "carrier": "release_absence_details projects the account onto real DomainDetail records with the EXISTING native.capability-unavailable code, delivered through DoctorResult.defects[] (existing doctor StepKind, x-opensip-order sequence) and StepTermination.domainDetail including on a SUCCESS step. AnalysisResult is NOT widened and no new DomainDetailCode is added.",
   "validated": "every detail, the DoctorResult and the success StepTermination admit through the real workflow schemas",
   "blanketPairResidue": "corrected in admission 1.1, native 10 UNSUPPORTED-TYPED and unsupportedTypedIsNotOnThisTable"
  },
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-PUBLIC-ROUTE-COMPLETE",
   "position": "agreed and corrected",
   "route": "public_termination_for(key, origin) derives a real StepTermination for all 18 branches; every one validates against the schema. Prose placeholders are deleted; domainDetail is present only where an existing closed member names the condition and explicitly ABSENT otherwise with the operational carrier named.",
   "classification": "external configuration -> request-rejected/CONFIG.INVALID; externally supplied or retained spec of known external origin -> request-rejected/REQUEST.PRECONDITION_FAILED; host BUG minting its own invalid internal layer -> operational-failed/SYSTEM.OUTCOME.ILLEGAL_STATE + faultCause host-invariant (nonAnalysisDerivation rule 5, domainCondition host-fault); authenticated release declaration -> request-rejected/REQUEST.PRECONDITION_FAILED; producer boundary -> operational-failed/PROVIDER.PROTOCOL_VIOLATION. A NOT-SELECTED cell is origin-independent: REQUEST.UNSATISFIABLE with the existing PROVIDER.NOT_SELECTED detail.",
   "successorNeedingRootAttention": {
    "what": "one D9FaultCause member `host-invariant` mapping to the EXISTING SYSTEM.OUTCOME.ILLEGAL_STATE",
    "why": "that error code was the SOLE orphan in the closed vocabulary - no faultCause and no rejectionCause mapped to it - while codeMaps.rule declares the maps total and injective and StepTermination requires operational-failed to carry both an errorCode and a non-none faultCause. A host-invariant fault was therefore unrepresentable, and borrowing host-io would be a semantically unrelated code.",
    "added": [
     "docs/coop/design-corrections/workflows/schemas/common.schema.json#/$defs/D9FaultCause",
     "docs/coop/design-corrections/workflows/workflows_model.v1.py FAULT_TO_ERROR"
    ],
    "notAdded": [
     "any error code",
     "any D9 class",
     "any exit code",
     "any reason code",
     "any public DomainDetailCode"
    ],
    "historicalBytes": "docs/coop/artifacts/d9-exit-contract.v1.14.json is UNCHANGED, so its own faultCause enum still omits the member; publishing the successor D9 artifact belongs to that unit and the source says so.",
    "flaggedForDecision": "This is the one place I could not complete without a vocabulary change. If Codex prefers no member, the honest alternative is that a host-invariant fault has NO representable termination and the contract must say so - but that leaves section 10 asserting a classification nothing can emit."
   },
   "aliases": "only the two genuinely CONTEXT-FREE keys are aliased - native.requested-capability-mode-not-selected -> PROVIDER.NOT_SELECTED and native.release-capability-undeclared -> native.capability-unavailable, both already registry members. The origin-dependent keys are deliberately absent because a context-free map cannot express them, and the aliasRule now says absence is a positive statement rather than an omission. My v2 claim that all 14 belonged there and the edit was mechanical was wrong."
  }
 ],
